Evan Soto: opened a small docs PR to add a JS SDK example showing graceful handling of 429 + Retry-After and falling back to a lower-rate tier. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1692. It also references the usage-dashboard panel and a short migration note about tier names.
Marina Gomez: nice. can you inline the minimal retry helper? we tend to prefer tiny examples that copy-paste. also please call out which endpoints return Retry-After vs quota headers.
Evan Soto: good call. i added this helper in the snippet: 
```js
async function callWithRetry(fn, attempts = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    const res = await fn();
    if (res.status !== 429) return res;
    const retry = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
    const wait = retry ? parseInt(retry, 10) * 1000 : (i + 1) * 500;
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
  }
  throw new Error('rate limited');
}
```
